    "metadata": {
      "name": "EventGraph",
      "description": "Do Once, Do N, Flip Flop and Multi Gate driven by a For Loop and a Sequence.",
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
      "modified_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z"
    },
    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "FLOW GATES\n\nThese nodes remember how often they were triggered, so they only make sense when something runs\nthem repeatedly. A For Loop fires the chain six times; inside, a Sequence feeds four demos:\n  Do Once: its Then fires only the first time.     Do N (n = 3): fires the first three times.\n  Flip Flop: alternates B, A, B, A, ... (first trigger is B).\n  Multi Gate: Output0, Output1, Output2, Output3, then wraps around to Output0.\nThe state is kept per instance, so two copies of this class never disturb each other.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -300.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          240.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "THE LOOP\nFor Loop (count 6) runs its Body six times. Everything to the right happens once per iteration, so the gate nodes see six triggers.",
        "position": [
          360.0,
          120.0
        ],
        "size": [
          570.0,
          100.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "loop",
          "seq"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "DO ONCE\nThen fires on the first trigger only (once_count ends at 1). Wire the reset pin to start over.",
        "position": [
          960.0,
          -90.0
        ],
        "size": [
          1060.0,
          90.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.9,
          0.55,
          0.15,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "once",
          "oc",
          "oc1",
          "oc_set"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-4",
        "text": "DO N\nThen fires for the first n=3 triggers only (n_count ends at 3).",
        "position": [
          960.0,
          250.0
        ],
        "size": [
          1060.0,
          90.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.6,
          0.3,
          0.75,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "don",
          "nc",
          "nc1",
          "nc_set"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-5",
        "text": "FLIP FLOP\nOutput A and output B take turns, B first. Six triggers append B A B A B A, so flips ends as \"BABABA\".",
        "position": [
          960.0,
          590.0
        ],
        "size": [
          1060.0,
          90.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "ff",
          "fg_A",
          "fc_A",
          "fs_A",
          "fg_B",
          "fc_B",
          "fs_B"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-6",
        "text": "MULTI GATE\nSteps through Output0..Output3 and wraps: six triggers give 0 1 2 3 0 1, so gates ends as \"012301\".",
        "position": [
          960.0,
          1100.0
        ],
        "size": [
          1060.0,
          90.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.8,
          0.25,
          0.25,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      }
    ],
